<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="What tixible.com does and doesn't use cookies for, and how that will change if it does."
  updated="July 2026"
>

<p>Short version: tixible.com does not currently set any advertising or tracking cookies. Here's the full picture.</p>

<h2>What we use today</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Analytics — no cookies.</strong> We use Plausible Analytics, which is cookie-free by design. It doesn't set a cookie, doesn't track you across sessions, and doesn't build a profile of you.</li>
  <li><strong>Newsletter — one third-party cookie, only if you use the form.</strong> Subscribing via our newsletter form opens a confirmation window hosted by our email provider, Buttondown, which may set its own functional cookie in that window. We don't control this directly; see Buttondown's own policy for details.</li>
  <li><strong>No advertising cookies, no cross-site tracking, no ad retargeting pixels.</strong> We don't use any of these.</li>
</ul>

<h2>If that changes</h2>
<p>If we ever add tools that do use cookies for analytics or tracking (for example, Google Analytics or session-recording tools), we will add a consent banner before any such script loads, and you'll be able to accept or decline non-essential cookies — with essential-only as the default until you choose. This page will be updated at the same time, with a new "last updated" date above.</p>

<h2>Managing cookies</h2>
<p>You can clear or block cookies at any time through your browser settings. Since we don't rely on cookies for core site functionality, doing so won't break anything on tixible.com.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@tixible.com">hello@tixible.com</a>.</p>

</LegalLayout>
